<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-shandora"><span class="enc-name">Ali Shandora</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Shandora was emir of Trarza, a Moorish emirate north of the Senegal River in present-day Mauritania, in the early 18th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-sher-khan-anchan"><span class="enc-name">Ali Sher Khan Anchan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Sher Khan Anchan was the most famous ruler of the Maqpon dynasty of Baltistan, reigning in the late 16th and early 17th centuries.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-tegin"><span class="enc-name">Ali Tegin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Tegin was a prince of the Kara-Khanid dynasty who ruled Bukhara and much of Transoxiana from about 1020 until his death in 1034.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-yaji"><span class="enc-name">Ali Yaji</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Yaji was ruler of the Hausa kingdom of Kano in the 14th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-yusuf-kenadid"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-yusuf-kenadid.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Yusuf Kenadid</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Yusuf Kenadid was the last sultan of Hobyo in central Somalia, succeeding his father Yusuf Ali Kenadid.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-qoli-khan-bakhtiari"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-qoli-khan-bakhtiari.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali-Qoli Khan Bakhtiari</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali-Qoli Khan Bakhtiari, known as Sardar As'ad II, was a chief of the