nc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Alta Verapaz is a department of northern Guatemala with its capital at Cobán, a region of humid highlands and forests inhabited largely by Q'eqchi' Maya.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/altai-mountains"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/altai-mountains.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Altai Mountains</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Altai Mountains are a mountain range in Central Asia where Russia, China, Mongolia and Kazakhstan meet.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/altamaha-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/altamaha-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Altamaha River</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Altamaha River in Georgia, United States, is formed by the meeting of the Oconee and Ocmulgee rivers and flows into the Atlantic near Darien.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/altan-khan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/altan-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Altan Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Altan Khan was leader of the Tümed Mongols, a grandson of Dayan Khan who raided Ming China for decades.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/altars-of-the-philaeni"><span class="enc-name">Altars of the Philaeni</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Altars of the Philaeni were an ancient landmark on the coast of the Gulf of Sidra in Libya that marked the boundary between the territory of Carthage and Greek…</span></a></li></ul>
